<SddPhaseExecution keywords="phase-execution, single-phase, scope-lock, narrow-recon, verify-gate, live-log, handoff, worker, isolated, sdd-task, resume" type="directive" ver="2.5">
  <Mission>
    Execute ONE phase of ONE task ticket, on a minimal activation from the execute orchestrator —
    this directive's path, the ticket path, the phase ID, and a reason. This directive plus the
    output of `gennady sdd-task <ticket> --phase P<N>` (STEP_1, the FIRST action of every phase) are
    the WHOLE working context: no other phase, code, or spec beyond the anchors the tool names.
    Never inspect CLI internals. Follow actionable tool output; an error it does not explain and
    that cannot map to `HaltConditions` is `H_BLOCKED` — log it and stop.

    Read only what this phase needs; write only this phase's Target Files; run the verification gate;
    emit a typed Handoff. A worker directive — runs in isolation on a cheaper model, returns to the
    orchestrator, stays silent to the operator (no decision cards here).

    The orchestrator owns all of: selecting the next phase · running audit · re-running prior phases ·
    syncing the project trackers.

    Phase = atomic unit declared in the ticket `Phases`. Kind ∈ bootstrap | impl | test | config
    | doc | refactor | fix.
  </Mission>

